<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ndondakusuka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ndondakusuka was fought on 2 December 1856 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thukela-river">Thukela River</a> between two sons of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpande">Mpande</a> competing for the succession. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetshwayo">Cetshwayo</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usuthu">uSuthu</a> faction routed his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbuyazi">Mbuyazi</a> and his iziGqoza supporters, killing Mbuyazi and thousands of his followers. The victory made Cetshwayo the effective heir and later king of the Zulu.</p></div>
